## What I did

Resumed `D-FOREIGN-REPLAY-UNGATED-IMAGES` (critical, #1 in the ledger) at **step 4a** — the fix for the two mount-time purge defects sess50 proved (CLAIM B: own-slot purge runs before `xlog_recover`; CLAIM C: cross-instance stale purge destroys a victim's authority mid-replay). GPT's ruling requires both fixed *before* the step-5 gate can be enabled.

No code shipped — this was code recon that changed the design.

## The finding that matters

Sess50 handed off an "implementation blocker": deferring the own-slot purge was said to require GPT's `RECOVERING_OLD_INCARNATION` self-conflict bypass, because a retained stale bit at a mode ≠ the requested one falls into the CAW wait, `v5_caw_holders_alive` reports the holder alive (it's our own heartbeating slot), and the wait extends to the 8-minute hardcap — the mount waits on itself, then fails.

That blocker dissolves. Three line-verified facts compose:

1. `caw_grant_epoch_update` (`dlm/dlm_caw.c:946`) stamps `ex_grant_epoch` **only for EX/PW** — PR/CR/CW grants carry no authority and are not part of the manifest.
2. The XFS overlay never requests PW or CW (occurrence counts in `xfs/xfs_mxfs_dlm.c`: EX×90, NL×62, PR×27, CR×1, PW×0, CW×0).
3. `node_held_mode` (`dlm_caw.c:433`) returns the **strongest** mode held.

So if mount purges our own stale PR/CR bits and retains only EX/PW, `our_mode` is NL or EX. EX ≥ every mode the FS can request, so every acquire lands on the `our_mode == mode` fast path or the `our_mode >= mode` subsume path — **both grant with no CAS, no `generation++`, and no epoch re-stamp**. Epoch preserved, no wait, no bypass needed.

Two other open questions closed by reading: a BAST cannot steal the retained bits (disk-poll scan iterates the *local* `ctx->held` array, empty on a fresh ctx; the UDP path reaches `mxfs_dlm_ag_bast_notify`, which only schedules a release when `pag_dlm_cached` is true). And the CLAIM-C purge cannot simply be deleted in favor of the monitor — `check_dead` requires `nt->live`, which a slot frozen before first sight never reaches, so those bits are unreachable by any other cleaner and must be *rerouted* into the D2 replay machinery rather than removed.

The design, the residual hazards to watch (`orphan_nak` under CAW), and the concrete 5-file edit list for 0.11.399 are in ccmemory as `ccloop-c7ee71c6-sess51-step4a-design-manifest-is-EX-only`.

